<title>FRANCE: Bouygues sees 1997 investment unchanged.</title>
<headline>Bouygues sees 1997 investment unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>French building group Bouygues expects investment to be about the same level as last year, finance director Olivier Poupard Lafarge said on Monday.</p>
<p>He said investment should also be roughly flat. Operating investment, which totaled 3.175 billion francs in 1996, should be &quot;quite close&quot; to that figure this year -- between 3.1 and 3.2 billion francs, Lafarge told a news conference.</p>
<p>Financial investment, which totaled 535 million francs last year, also should be around last year's level, he added.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
